    "its range and records the bounds it was asked for; see that tool's emitDrops.",
    "`item` is what the block leaves behind, 0 for nothing. `itemByMetadata` is",
    "present only when the answer depends on the metadata -- a door's upper half",
    "drops nothing, a crop drops only when it is grown. `altItem`/`altOneIn` is",
    "the second answer and its odds: nextInt(altOneIn) == 0 picks it, which is",
    "gravel's flint and nothing else in this version. `countMin` is how many drop,",
    "`countSpread` adds nextInt(countSpread) to it, and `countOneIn` is the other",
    "form -- nextInt(countOneIn) == 0 ? countMin : 0, which is a leaf block.",
    "There is no damage column: dropBlockAsItemWithChance builds new ItemStack(id),",
    "so a1.1.2 drops every block at damage zero."
  ],
